hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24275","Waki' and Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, both saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Salim Abu al-Nadr, from Busr ibn Sa'id, that Zayd ibn Khalid sent to Abu Juhaym, Abd al-Rahman said: Zayd ibn Khalid sent me to Abu Juhaym al-Ansari: What did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say regarding a man passing in front of a man while he is praying? He said: I heard him say: If one of you knew what is upon him in passing in front of a man while he is praying, for him to stand forty, I do not know: A year, or a day, or a month, would be better for him than that."
"24276","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Malik informed us, from Abu al-Nadr, from Busr ibn Sa'id, who said: Zayd ibn Khalid sent me to Abu Juhaym al-Ansari to ask him: What did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say regarding one who passes in front of one praying? He said: I heard him say: For him to stand in his place is better for him than to pass in front of one praying. I do not know whether he said: Forty years, or forty months, or forty days."
"24277","Ya'qub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, Abd al-Rahman ibn Hurmuz al-A'raj narrated to me, from Umayr, freedman of Abdullah ibn Abbas, and Umayr, freedman of Abdullah ibn Abbas, was trustworthy in what reached me, from Abu Juhaym ibn al-Harith ibn al-Simmah al-Ansari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out for some need toward the well of Jamal, then came back, and a man from among his companions met him and greeted him. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not return the greeting to him until he placed his hand on the wall, then wiped his face and his hands, then said: And upon you be peace."
